    "body": "@zcorpan for iframes, it should be that the \"update the rendering\" steps for skipped iframes does not happen. It's similar to how cross-origin iframes that are not on-screen can skip their \"update the rendering\" steps.\r\n\r\nShouldn't this be relatively simple to specify? Essentially update the sentence that says \"Remove from docs all Document objects for which the user agent believes that it's preferrable to skip updating the rendering for other reasons.\" to instead say \"Remove from docs all Document updates for which one of the following is true:\r\n\r\n* The iframe is cross-origin to its parent (or the appropriate equivalent spec language) and is not visible to the user\r\n* The iframe is skipped [link to css-contain spec]\r\n* The user agent believes it is preferable to skip updating the rendering",
